<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Aug 1996.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Aug 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports last month, despite a strong decline in traffic on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>August 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 3,298 tonnes, down 26.0 percent on the same month last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 2,234 tonnes, an increase of 6.8 percent on August 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 2,089 tonnes flown ex-Paris last month, up of 16.6 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in August 1996 and the percentage change on August 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	 3,298 tonnes    (-26.0 pct)</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	  2,234 tonnes     (+6.8)</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	2,089 tonnes    (+16.6)</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	    1,992 tonnes    (-20.1)</p>
<p> 5  Mexico City    1,068 tonnes    (+40.5)</p>
<p> 6  Sao Paulo	1,067 tonnes    (+16.6)</p>
<p> 7  Miami	    1,005 tonnes   (+196.3)</p>
<p> 8  Los Angeles	743 tonnes    (-10.4)</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		723 tonnes    (-12.2)</p>
<p> 10 Montreal	   650 tonnes     (-6.9)</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
